At this point in time we have 2 algorithms when we discuss small order fee calculations:

* Regular SOF calculation;
* Dynamic SOF;

We need to introduce another algorithm, “Laddered SOF”. 

How should we decide which algorithm is used?

* The best choice would be to have a dropdown on provider page, to choose the algorithm;
* We can override this choice on targeting level;

We should rethink the config format that is used now and include the possibility to test both marketing and food verticals. I will focus on this task on [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DCE-3885|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DCE-3885|smart-link] 


The proposed implementation, for MVP (Release 1):

* Define JSON config for targeting (possibly using a new targeting event, TBD);
* Implement algorithm;
* Changes on eater-basket side:
** Display laddered thresholds;
** Update request / response contracts;
* Testing phase;



Proposed features, for Release 2:

* Save in DB those generated SOF values for traceability;
* Add provider-level config;
* Update code to include provider settings;



I think that the initial estimation, of 6 weeks is enough.

