Hi [~accountid:6052892937065a00698bdafa] There are no major obstacles from the legal side, just points to consider:

* the attached contract is a barter agreement:
** Flixbus generates individual discount codes (vouchers) for its services, Bolt undertakes to distribute vouchers and advertise to each other; so there is no money flow - everything is compensated - the barter set-up to be verified with our tax team;
** note that there are no commitments in the contract relating to Bolt's mobility stations at Flixbus stations (which you mention below) - if this is to be included, additional changes to the template are required;
* the distribution of vouchers would need to be examined in terms of its compliance with the Omnibus Directive (whether this places an obligation on Bolt to provide the 30-day lowest price for Bolt services, or any Bolt's responsibility in this regard); 
** in the current template - Flixbus issues vouchers for its services and Bolt distributes them to its customers - my initial view is that this should not give rise to any liability on the part of Bolt as these are not discounts on our services (to be verified);
** however, if we decide to issue our vouchers and make them available to Flixbus customers, then the Omnibus obligation may apply (to be verified);

Please let me know if you have any questions or if any further analysis is required at this stage.

